msgid ""
"If you're on macOS 26, try `xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:118
msgid "Cargo errors claiming that a dependency is using unstable features"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:120
msgid "Try `cargo clean` and `cargo build`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:122
msgid "Error: 'dispatch/dispatch.h' file not found"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:124
msgid "If you encounter an error similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:127
msgid "'dispatch/dispatch.h'"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:130
msgid ""
"'t exit successfully\n"
"\n"
"  --- stdout\n"
"  cargo:rustc-link-lib=framework=System\n"
"  cargo:rerun-if-changed=src/platform/mac/dispatch.h\n"
"  cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=TARGET\n"
"  cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS_aarch64-apple-darwin\n"
"  cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS_aarch64_apple_darwin\n"
"  cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:141
msgid ""
"This file is part of Xcode. Ensure you have installed the Xcode command line "
"tools and set the correct path:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:148
msgid "Additionally, set the `BINDGEN_EXTRA_CLANG_ARGS` environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:151
msgid "\"--sysroot=$(xcrun --show-sdk-path)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:154
msgid "Then clean and rebuild the project:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:161
msgid "Tests failing due to `Too many open files (os error 24)`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:163
msgid ""
"This error seems to be caused by OS resource constraints. Installing and "
"running tests with `cargo-nextest` should resolve the issue."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:165
msgid "`cargo install cargo-nextest --locked`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:166
msgid "`cargo nextest run --workspace --no-fail-fast`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:168
msgid "Tips & Tricks"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:170
msgid "Avoiding continual rebuilds"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:172
msgid ""
"If you are finding that Zed is continually rebuilding root crates, it may be "
"because you are pointing your development Zed at the codebase itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:175
msgid ""
"This causes problems because `cargo run` exports a bunch of environment "
"variables which are picked up by the `rust-analyzer` that runs in the "
"development build of Zed. These environment variables are in turn passed to "
"`cargo check`, which invalidates the build cache of some of the crates we "
"depend on."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:180
msgid ""
"You can easily avoid running the built binary on the checked-out Zed "
"codebase using `cargo run ~/path/to/other/project` to ensure that you don't "
"hit this."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:183
msgid "Speeding up verification"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:185
msgid ""
"If you are building Zed a lot, you may find that macOS continually verifies "
"new builds which can add a few seconds to your iteration cycles."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:188
msgid "To fix this, you can:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:190
msgid ""
"Run `sudo spctl developer-mode enable-terminal` to enable the Developer "
"Tools panel in System Settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:191
msgid ""
"In System Settings, search for \"Developer Tools\" and add your terminal (e."
"g. iTerm or Ghostty) to the list under \"Allow applications to use developer "
"tools\""
msgstr ""

#: src/development/macos.md:192
msgid "Restart your terminal."
msgstr "重新啟動終端機。"

